# Third-party notices

SiftX is distributed as a compiled native library that links the Rust crates
listed below. Their licences require their copyright notices to travel with any
redistribution, which is what this file is for.

Generated from the resolved dependency graph with
[cargo-about](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about); regenerate with:

```bash
cargo about generate --fail about.hbs | tr -d '\r' > THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
```

SiftX itself is `MIT OR Apache-2.0`; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).

{{!--
  cargo-about has no way to exclude the root crate: `private.ignore` only drops
  crates marked `publish = false`, and truespar-siftx is meant to be published. Without
  this guard truespar-siftx lists its own LICENSE-APACHE among the third-party notices,
  which is the one entry that does not belong in a third-party file. truespar-siftx's own
  licence text always forms a group of its own, so matching a single-crate
  group named "truespar-siftx" is enough; if that ever stopped holding, the worst case is
  truespar-siftx reappearing in the list, not a crate going unattributed.
--}}
